-- Cryptography and Network Security | ESE | easy | 4900932005030125 | theory
INSERT INTO public."TestsData" ("TestId", "Questions", "Options", "Answers")
VALUES (4900932005030125, ARRAY['"[8 marks] Explain Need for Security in the context of Security in Computing Environment. Define it, describe the key principles or steps, and give one relevant practical example."'::jsonb, '"[8 marks] Explain Terminologies used in Cryptography in the context of Basics of Cryptography. Define it, describe the key principles or steps, and give one relevant practical example."'::jsonb, '"[8 marks] Explain Block Ciphers in the context of Symmetric Key Encryption. Define it, describe the key principles or steps, and give one relevant practical example."'::jsonb, '"[8 marks] Explain Integer Factorization Problems in the context of Public Key Encryption. Define it, describe the key principles or steps, and give one relevant practical example."'::jsonb]::jsonb[], ARRAY[]::jsonb[], ARRAY['"Model answer (8 marks)\n\n**Meaning and purpose (2 marks):** Need for Security appears in “Security in Computing Environment”. Define its role and features, relate it to Security Attack – Threats, Vulnerabilities, and Controls, Types of Threats (Attacks), provide a practical example and state one process/design check or limitation. Confirm the details against official teaching material.\n\n**Principles/procedure (3 marks):** Explain the concept in logical order and relate it to Security Attack – Threats, Vulnerabilities, and Controls, Types of Threats (Attacks), Security Services – Confidentiality. Include the relevant conditions, components, operating variables or formulas.\n\n**Application/example (2 marks):** Apply it to a concrete Cryptography and Network Security task and describe the expected result.\n\n**Verification/conclusion (1 mark):** Check against the stated objective and mention a limitation, error source or safety/design trade-off.\n\nMarking guide: meaning 2; principles/steps 3; application 2; verification 1. Confirm against official teaching material before use."'::jsonb, '"Model answer (8 marks)\n\n**Meaning and purpose (2 marks):** Terminologies used in Cryptography appears in “Basics of Cryptography”. Define its role and features, relate it to Substitution Techniques – The Caesar Cipher, One-Time Pads, The Vernam Cipher, Book Cipher, provide a practical example and state one process/design check or limitation. Confirm the details against official teaching material.\n\n**Principles/procedure (3 marks):** Explain the concept in logical order and relate it to Substitution Techniques – The Caesar Cipher, One-Time Pads, The Vernam Cipher, Book Cipher, Transposition Techniques – Encipherment/Decipherment Complexity. Include the relevant conditions, components, operating variables or formulas.\n\n**Application/example (2 marks):** Apply it to a concrete Cryptography and Network Security task and describe the expected result.\n\n**Verification/conclusion (1 mark):** Check against the stated objective and mention a limitation, error source or safety/design trade-off.\n\nMarking guide: meaning 2; principles/steps 3; application 2; verification 1. Confirm against official teaching material before use."'::jsonb, '"Model answer (8 marks)\n\n**Meaning and purpose (2 marks):** Block Ciphers appears in “Symmetric Key Encryption”. Define its role and features, relate it to Cipher Block Chaining Mode, Data Encryption Standard (DES) Algorithm – Overview of the DES Algorithm, Double and Triple DES – Double DES, Triple DES, provide a practical example and state one process/design check or limitation. Confirm the details against official teaching material.\n\n**Principles/procedure (3 marks):** Explain the concept in logical order and relate it to Cipher Block Chaining Mode, Data Encryption Standard (DES) Algorithm – Overview of the DES Algorithm, Double and Triple DES – Double DES, Triple DES, Security of the DES. Include the relevant conditions, components, operating variables or formulas.\n\n**Application/example (2 marks):** Apply it to a concrete Cryptography and Network Security task and describe the expected result.\n\n**Verification/conclusion (1 mark):** Check against the stated objective and mention a limitation, error source or safety/design trade-off.\n\nMarking guide: meaning 2; principles/steps 3; application 2; verification 1. Confirm against official teaching material before use."'::jsonb, '"Model answer (8 marks)\n\n**Meaning and purpose (2 marks):** Integer Factorization Problems appears in “Public Key Encryption”. Define its role and features, relate it to Characteristics of Public Key System, RSA Technique – Encryption-Method, Key Exchange, Diffie-Hellman Scheme, provide a practical example and state one process/design check or limitation. Confirm the details against official teaching material.\n\n**Principles/procedure (3 marks):** Explain the concept in logical order and relate it to Characteristics of Public Key System, RSA Technique – Encryption-Method, Key Exchange, Diffie-Hellman Scheme, ElGamal. Include the relevant conditions, components, operating variables or formulas.\n\n**Application/example (2 marks):** Apply it to a concrete Cryptography and Network Security task and describe the expected result.\n\n**Verification/conclusion (1 mark):** Check against the stated objective and mention a limitation, error source or safety/design trade-off.\n\nMarking guide: meaning 2; principles/steps 3; application 2; verification 1. Confirm against official teaching material before use."'::jsonb]::jsonb[]);

