VALUES (4900932005030135, ARRAY['"[8 marks] Analyze a realistic task involving Need for Security in Cryptography and Network Security. Explain the governing principle, justify the method or selection, and include a verification check and limitation."'::jsonb, '"[8 marks] Analyze a realistic task involving Terminologies used in Cryptography in Cryptography and Network Security. Explain the governing principle, justify the method or selection, and include a verification check and limitation."'::jsonb, '"[8 marks] Analyze a realistic task involving Security Attack – Threats in Cryptography and Network Security. Explain the governing principle, justify the method or selection, and include a verification check and limitation."'::jsonb, '"[8 marks] Analyze a realistic task involving Vulnerabilities in Cryptography and Network Security. Explain the governing principle, justify the method or selection, and include a verification check and limitation."'::jsonb]::jsonb[], ARRAY[]::jsonb[], ARRAY['"Model answer (8 marks)\n\n**Meaning and purpose (2 marks):** Need for Security appears in “Security in Computing Environment”. Define its role and features, relate it to Security Attack – Threats, Vulnerabilities, and Controls, Types of Threats (Attacks), provide a practical example and state one process/design check or limitation. Confirm the details against official teaching material.\n\n**Principles/procedure (3 marks):** Explain the concept in logical order and relate it to Security Attack – Threats, Vulnerabilities, and Controls, Types of Threats (Attacks), Security Services – Confidentiality. Include the relevant conditions, components, operating variables or formulas.\n\n**Application/example (2 marks):** Apply it to a concrete Cryptography and Network Security task and describe the expected result.\n\n**Verification/conclusion (1 mark):** Check against the stated objective and mention a limitation, error source or safety/design trade-off.\n\nMarking guide: meaning 2; principles/steps 3; application 2; verification 1. Confirm against official teaching material before use."'::jsonb, '"Model answer (8 marks)\n\n**Meaning and purpose (2 marks):** Terminologies used in Cryptography appears in “Basics of Cryptography”. Define its role and features, relate it to Substitution Techniques – The Caesar Cipher, One-Time Pads, The Vernam Cipher, Book Cipher, provide a practical example and state one process/design check or limitation. Confirm the details against official teaching material.\n\n**Principles/procedure (3 marks):** Explain the concept in logical order and relate it to Substitution Techniques – The Caesar Cipher, One-Time Pads, The Vernam Cipher, Book Cipher, Transposition Techniques – Encipherment/Decipherment Complexity. Include the relevant conditions, components, operating variables or formulas.\n\n**Application/example (2 marks):** Apply it to a concrete Cryptography and Network Security task and describe the expected result.\n\n**Verification/conclusion (1 mark):** Check against the stated objective and mention a limitation, error source or safety/design trade-off.\n\nMarking guide: meaning 2; principles/steps 3; application 2; verification 1. Confirm against official teaching material before use."'::jsonb, '"Model answer (8 marks)\n\n**Meaning and purpose (2 marks):** Security Attack – Threats appears in “Security in Computing Environment”. Define its role and features, relate it to Need for Security, Vulnerabilities, and Controls, Types of Threats (Attacks), provide a practical example and state one process/design check or limitation. Confirm the details against official teaching material.\n\n**Principles/procedure (3 marks):** Explain the concept in logical order and relate it to Need for Security, Vulnerabilities, and Controls, Types of Threats (Attacks), Security Services – Confidentiality. Include the relevant conditions, components, operating variables or formulas.\n\n**Application/example (2 marks):** Apply it to a concrete Cryptography and Network Security task and describe the expected result.\n\n**Verification/conclusion (1 mark):** Check against the stated objective and mention a limitation, error source or safety/design trade-off.\n\nMarking guide: meaning 2; principles/steps 3; application 2; verification 1. Confirm against official teaching material before use."'::jsonb, '"Model answer (8 marks)\n\n**Meaning and purpose (2 marks):** Vulnerabilities appears in “Security in Computing Environment”. Define its role and features, relate it to Need for Security, Security Attack – Threats, and Controls, Types of Threats (Attacks), provide a practical example and state one process/design check or limitation. Confirm the details against official teaching material.\n\n**Principles/procedure (3 marks):** Explain the concept in logical order and relate it to Need for Security, Security Attack – Threats, and Controls, Types of Threats (Attacks), Security Services – Confidentiality. Include the relevant conditions, components, operating variables or formulas.\n\n**Application/example (2 marks):** Apply it to a concrete Cryptography and Network Security task and describe the expected result.\n\n**Verification/conclusion (1 mark):** Check against the stated objective and mention a limitation, error source or safety/design trade-off.\n\nMarking guide: meaning 2; principles/steps 3; application 2; verification 1. Confirm against official teaching material before use."'::jsonb]::jsonb[]);

