VALUES (490093200512016, ARRAY['"[8 marks] A practical problem in Linux Administrator involves the syllabus topic bash introduction as applied within Managing Files from the Command Line. Explain how BASH introduction applies, outline the steps and justify the result with an example."'::jsonb, '"[8 marks] A practical problem in Linux Administrator involves the syllabus topic creating users as applied within Managing Users and Groups. Explain how Creating users applies, outline the steps and justify the result with an example."'::jsonb, '"[8 marks] A practical problem in Linux Administrator involves the syllabus topic output redirection as applied within Shell Processing and Task Scheduling. Explain how Output redirection applies, outline the steps and justify the result with an example."'::jsonb, '"[8 marks] A practical problem in Linux Administrator involves the syllabus topic installing linux as applied within Basics of Linux. Explain how installing Linux applies, outline the steps and justify the result with an example."'::jsonb]::jsonb[], ARRAY[]::jsonb[], ARRAY['"Model answer (8 marks)\n\n**Meaning and purpose (2 marks):** BASH introduction appears in “Managing Files from the Command Line”. Define its role and features, relate it to command line shortcuts, file types, file ownership, file permissions, provide a practical example and state one process/design check or limitation. Confirm the details against official teaching material.\n\n**Principles/procedure (3 marks):** Explain the concept in logical order and relate it to command line shortcuts, file types, file ownership, file permissions, file management and manipulation. Include the relevant conditions, components, operating variables or formulas.\n\n**Application/example (2 marks):** Apply it to a concrete Linux Administrator task and describe the expected result.\n\n**Verification/conclusion (1 mark):** Check against the stated objective and mention a limitation, error source or safety/design trade-off.\n\nMarking guide: meaning 2; principles/steps 3; application 2; verification 1. Confirm against official teaching material before use."'::jsonb, '"Model answer (8 marks)\n\n**Meaning and purpose (2 marks):** Creating users appears in “Managing Users and Groups”. Define its role and features, relate it to managing users, user management tools, creating groups, access permissions, provide a practical example and state one process/design check or limitation. Confirm the details against official teaching material.\n\n**Principles/procedure (3 marks):** Explain the concept in logical order and relate it to managing users, user management tools, creating groups, access permissions, editing group attributes. Include the relevant conditions, components, operating variables or formulas.\n\n**Application/example (2 marks):** Apply it to a concrete Linux Administrator task and describe the expected result.\n\n**Verification/conclusion (1 mark):** Check against the stated objective and mention a limitation, error source or safety/design trade-off.\n\nMarking guide: meaning 2; principles/steps 3; application 2; verification 1. Confirm against official teaching material before use."'::jsonb, '"Model answer (8 marks)\n\n**Meaning and purpose (2 marks):** Output redirection appears in “Shell Processing and Task Scheduling”. Define its role and features, relate it to input and output redirection, pipelines, editing text files from shell, cron scheduling, provide a practical example and state one process/design check or limitation. Confirm the details against official teaching material.\n\n**Principles/procedure (3 marks):** Explain the concept in logical order and relate it to input and output redirection, pipelines, editing text files from shell, cron scheduling, task automation. Include the relevant conditions, components, operating variables or formulas.\n\n**Application/example (2 marks):** Apply it to a concrete Linux Administrator task and describe the expected result.\n\n**Verification/conclusion (1 mark):** Check against the stated objective and mention a limitation, error source or safety/design trade-off.\n\nMarking guide: meaning 2; principles/steps 3; application 2; verification 1. Confirm against official teaching material before use."'::jsonb, '"Model answer (8 marks)\n\n**Meaning and purpose (2 marks):** installing Linux appears in “Basics of Linux”. Define its role and features, relate it to History of GNU Linux, updating software, managing packages, Red Hat repositories, provide a practical example and state one process/design check or limitation. Confirm the details against official teaching material.\n\n**Principles/procedure (3 marks):** Explain the concept in logical order and relate it to History of GNU Linux, updating software, managing packages, Red Hat repositories, yum package repositories. Include the relevant conditions, components, operating variables or formulas.\n\n**Application/example (2 marks):** Apply it to a concrete Linux Administrator task and describe the expected result.\n\n**Verification/conclusion (1 mark):** Check against the stated objective and mention a limitation, error source or safety/design trade-off.\n\nMarking guide: meaning 2; principles/steps 3; application 2; verification 1. Confirm against official teaching material before use."'::jsonb]::jsonb[]);

