icrocontroller, Features of microcontroller, Evolution of microcontroller, Difference between microprocessor and microcontroller, provide a practical example and state one process/design check or limitation. Confirm the details against official teaching material.\n\n**Principles/procedure (3 marks):** Explain the concept in logical order and relate it to Block diagram of microcontroller, Features of microcontroller, Evolution of microcontroller, Difference between microprocessor and microcontroller, Microcontroller architecture- Von neuman and Harward architecture. Include the relevant conditions, components, operating variables or formulas.\n\n**Application/example (2 marks):** Apply it to a concrete Microcontroller and Interfacing task and describe the expected result.\n\n**Verification/conclusion (1 mark):** Check against the stated objective and mention a limitation, error source or safety/design trade-off.\n\nMarking guide: meaning 2; principles/steps 3; application 2; verification 1. Confirm against official teaching material before use."'::jsonb, '"Model answer (8 marks)\n\n**Meaning and purpose (2 marks):** Pin Diagram of 8051 appears in “Introduction to Microcontroller”. Define its role and features, relate it to Block diagram of microcontroller, Features of microcontroller, Evolution of microcontroller, Difference between microprocessor and microcontroller, provide a practical example and state one process/design check or limitation. Confirm the details against official teaching material.\n\n**Principles/procedure (3 marks):** Explain the concept in logical order and relate it to Block diagram of microcontroller, Features of microcontroller, Evolution of microcontroller, Difference between microprocessor and microcontroller, Microcontroller architecture- Von neuman and Harward architecture. Include the relevant conditions, components, operating variables or formulas.\n\n**Application/example (2 marks):** Apply it to a concrete Microcontroller and Interfacing task and describe the expected result.\n\n**Verification/conclusion (1 mark):** Check against the stated objective and mention a limitation, error source or safety/design trade-off.\n\nMarking guide: meaning 2; principles/steps 3; application 2; verification 1. Confirm against official teaching material before use."'::jsonb]::jsonb[]);

