VALUES (4900932005010125, ARRAY['"[8 marks] Explain Types of statistics in the context of Statistics and Descriptive Methods. Define it, describe the key principles or steps, and give one relevant practical example."'::jsonb, '"[8 marks] Explain Data in the context of Graphical and Tabular Descriptive Techniques. Define it, describe the key principles or steps, and give one relevant practical example."'::jsonb, '"[8 marks] Explain Mean in the context of Numerical Descriptive Techniques. Define it, describe the key principles or steps, and give one relevant practical example."'::jsonb, '"[8 marks] Explain Methods of data collection in the context of Data Collection and Sampling. Define it, describe the key principles or steps, and give one relevant practical example."'::jsonb]::jsonb[], ARRAY[]::jsonb[], ARRAY['"Model answer (8 marks)\n\n**Meaning and purpose (2 marks):** Types of statistics appears in “Statistics and Descriptive Methods”. Define its role and features, relate it to applications of statistical analysis, population, sample, statistical inference, provide a practical example and state one process/design check or limitation. Confirm the details against official teaching material.\n\n**Principles/procedure (3 marks):** Explain the concept in logical order and relate it to applications of statistical analysis, population, sample, statistical inference, Statistics and Descriptive Methods. Include the relevant conditions, components, operating variables or formulas.\n\n**Application/example (2 marks):** Apply it to a concrete Probability and Statistics task and describe the expected result.\n\n**Verification/conclusion (1 mark):** Check against the stated objective and mention a limitation, error source or safety/design trade-off.\n\nMarking guide: meaning 2; principles/steps 3; application 2; verification 1. Confirm against official teaching material before use."'::jsonb, '"Model answer (8 marks)\n\n**Meaning and purpose (2 marks):** Data appears in “Graphical and Tabular Descriptive Techniques”. Define its role and features, relate it to frequency distribution, data representation, pie charts, bar charts, provide a practical example and state one process/design check or limitation. Confirm the details against official teaching material.\n\n**Principles/procedure (3 marks):** Explain the concept in logical order and relate it to frequency distribution, data representation, pie charts, bar charts, histograms. Include the relevant conditions, components, operating variables or formulas.\n\n**Application/example (2 marks):** Apply it to a concrete Probability and Statistics task and describe the expected result.\n\n**Verification/conclusion (1 mark):** Check against the stated objective and mention a limitation, error source or safety/design trade-off.\n\nMarking guide: meaning 2; principles/steps 3; application 2; verification 1. Confirm against official teaching material before use."'::jsonb, '"Model answer (8 marks)\n\n**Meaning and purpose (2 marks):** Mean appears in “Numerical Descriptive Techniques”. Define its role and features, relate it to median, mode, averages, variance, provide a practical example and state one process/design check or limitation. Confirm the details against official teaching material.\n\n**Principles/procedure (3 marks):** Explain the concept in logical order and relate it to median, mode, averages, variance, standard deviation. Include the relevant conditions, components, operating variables or formulas.\n\n**Application/example (2 marks):** Apply it to a concrete Probability and Statistics task and describe the expected result.\n\n**Verification/conclusion (1 mark):** Check against the stated objective and mention a limitation, error source or safety/design trade-off.\n\nMarking guide: meaning 2; principles/steps 3; application 2; verification 1. Confirm against official teaching material before use."'::jsonb, '"Model answer (8 marks)\n\n**Meaning and purpose (2 marks):** Methods of data collection appears in “Data Collection and Sampling”. Define its role and features, relate it to sampling, sampling plans, sampling errors, non-sampling errors, provide a practical example and state one process/design check or limitation. Confirm the details against official teaching material.\n\n**Principles/procedure (3 marks):** Explain the concept in logical order and relate it to sampling, sampling plans, sampling errors, non-sampling errors, sampling distribution of the mean. Include the relevant conditions, components, operating variables or formulas.\n\n**Application/example (2 marks):** Apply it to a concrete Probability and Statistics task and describe the expected result.\n\n**Verification/conclusion (1 mark):** Check against the stated objective and mention a limitation, error source or safety/design trade-off.\n\nMarking guide: meaning 2; principles/steps 3; application 2; verification 1. Confirm against official teaching material before use."'::jsonb]::jsonb[]);

