ncrete VLSI task and describe the expected result.\n\n**Verification/conclusion (1 mark):** Check against the stated objective and mention a limitation, error source or safety/design trade-off.\n\nMarking guide: meaning 2; principles/steps 3; application 2; verification 1. Confirm against official teaching material before use."'::jsonb, '"Model answer (8 marks)\n\n**Meaning and purpose (2 marks):** CMOS SR latch based on 2-input NOR gates appears in “Sequential MOS logic circuits”. Define its role and features, relate it to CMOS SR latch based on 2-input NAND gates, Clocked SR latch, Clocked JK latch, JK Master-Slave flip-flops, provide a practical example and state one process/design check or limitation. Confirm the details against official teaching material.\n\n**Principles/procedure (3 marks):** Explain the concept in logical order and relate it to CMOS SR latch based on 2-input NAND gates, Clocked SR latch, Clocked JK latch, JK Master-Slave flip-flops, CMOS D-latch and edge triggered D-flip-flop. Include the relevant conditions, components, operating variables or formulas.\n\n**Application/example (2 marks):** Apply it to a concrete VLSI task and describe the expected result.\n\n**Verification/conclusion (1 mark):** Check against the stated objective and mention a limitation, error source or safety/design trade-off.\n\nMarking guide: meaning 2; principles/steps 3; application 2; verification 1. Confirm against official teaching material before use."'::jsonb, '"Model answer (8 marks)\n\n**Meaning and purpose (2 marks):** VLSI design flow appears in “Introduction to VLSI Design”. Define its role and features, relate it to Historical perspective, Design Methodologies, Y- chart, Full custom design, provide a practical example and state one process/design check or limitation. Confirm the details against official teaching material.\n\n**Principles/procedure (3 marks):** Explain the concept in logical order and relate it to Historical perspective, Design Methodologies,