VALUES (4900932005100112, ARRAY['"[8 marks] Analyze a realistic task involving VLSI design flow in VLSI. Explain the governing principle, justify the method or selection, and include a verification check and limitation."'::jsonb, '"[8 marks] Analyze a realistic task involving Design Methodologies in VLSI. Explain the governing principle, justify the method or selection, and include a verification check and limitation."'::jsonb, '"[8 marks] Analyze a realistic task involving Y- chart in VLSI. Explain the governing principle, justify the method or selection, and include a verification check and limitation."'::jsonb, '"[8 marks] Analyze a realistic task involving Full custom design in VLSI. Explain the governing principle, justify the method or selection, and include a verification check and limitation."'::jsonb]::jsonb[], ARRAY[]::jsonb[], ARRAY['"Model answer (8 marks)\n\n**Meaning and purpose (2 marks):** VLSI design flow appears in “Introduction to VLSI Design”. Define its role and features, relate it to Historical perspective, Design Methodologies, Y- chart, Full custom design, provide a practical example and state one process/design check or limitation. Confirm the details against official teaching material.\n\n**Principles/procedure (3 marks):** Explain the concept in logical order and relate it to Historical perspective, Design Methodologies, Y- chart, Full custom design, standard cell based design. Include the relevant conditions, components, operating variables or formulas.\n\n**Application/example (2 marks):** Apply it to a concrete VLSI task and describe the expected result.\n\n**Verification/conclusion (1 mark):** Check against the stated objective and mention a limitation, error source or safety/design trade-off.\n\nMarking guide: meaning 2; principles/steps 3; application 2; verification 1. Confirm against official teaching material before use."'::jsonb, '"Model answer (8 marks)\n\n**Meaning and purpose (2 marks):** Design Methodologies appears in “Introduction to VLSI Design”. Define its role and features, relate it to Historical perspective, VLSI design flow, Y- chart, Full custom design, provide a practical example and state one process/design check or limitation. Confirm the details against official teaching material.\n\n**Principles/procedure (3 marks):** Explain the concept in logical order and relate it to Historical perspective, VLSI design flow, Y- chart, Full custom design, standard cell based design. Include the relevant conditions, components, operating variables or formulas.\n\n**Application/example (2 marks):** Apply it to a concrete VLSI task and describe the expected result.\n\n**Verification/conclusion (1 mark):** Check against the stated objective and mention a limitation, error source or safety/design trade-off.\n\nMarking guide: meaning 2; principles/steps 3; application 2; verification 1. Confirm against official teaching material before use."'::jsonb, '"Model answer (8 marks)\n\n**Meaning and purpose (2 marks):** Y- chart appears in “Introduction to VLSI Design”. Define its role and features, relate it to Historical perspective, VLSI design flow, Design Methodologies, Full custom design, provide a practical example and state one process/design check or limitation. Confirm the details against official teaching material.\n\n**Principles/procedure (3 marks):** Explain the concept in logical order and relate it to Historical perspective, VLSI design flow, Design Methodologies, Full custom design, standard cell based design. Include the relevant conditions, components, operating variables or formulas.\n\n**Application/example (2 marks):** Apply it to a concrete VLSI task and describe the expected result.\n\n**Verification/conclusion (1 mark):** Check against the stated objective and mention a limitation, error source or safety/design trade-off.\n\nMarking guide: meaning 2; principles/steps 3; application 2; verification 1. Confirm against official teaching material before use."'::jsonb, '"Model answer (8 marks)\n\n**Meaning and purpose (2 marks):** Full custom design appears in “Introduction to VLSI Design”. Define its role and features, relate it to Historical perspective, VLSI design flow, Design Methodologies, Y- chart, provide a practical example and state one process/design check or limitation. Confirm the details against official teaching material.\n\n**Principles/procedure (3 marks):** Explain the concept in logical order and relate it to Historical perspective, VLSI design flow, Design Methodologies, Y- chart, standard cell based design. Include the relevant conditions, components, operating variables or formulas.\n\n**Application/example (2 marks):** Apply it to a concrete VLSI task and describe the expected result.\n\n**Verification/conclusion (1 mark):** Check against the stated objective and mention a limitation, error source or safety/design trade-off.\n\nMarking guide: meaning 2; principles/steps 3; application 2; verification 1. Confirm against official teaching material before use."'::jsonb]::jsonb[]);

